# Copy edit & Content pane

Highest-risk area for **“it works until I type”** bugs.

## Invariants (from `plateContentSave.ts`, `text.ts`, `plateContentPane.ts`)

- **Typing never bakes HTML** mid-keystroke. Bake on **leave plate**, structural save, or deferred schedule — not per key.
- **Content pane saves must not remount** the pane — remount **kills the caret**.
- **Copy saves must not remount** Content pane when stage paints from pane typing (break circular flash).
- **Soft-merge** content from live save — never replace full edit deck cache from one field echo.
- Pending reload queue: **never** stage-reload while a Content input is **focused**.
- Click-in-place edit: **timeline must not move** when focusing a field on stage.
- Deferred look/style paints: **keep playhead** — don’t jump to open on style change.

## Line layout (multi-line titles)

- Shared **`copyEdit.ts`** / **`copyEdit.js`**: lines → `.title-line` HTML; keep JS + TS ports aligned.
- Before `studio-edit`: **`captureAllLineLayouts`** (measured box height/gap); **`applyLineLayout`** on rows — not raw CSS `line-height` from type-fit alone.
- Don’t clear type-fit **`fontSize`** when applying line layout fixes.

## UX expectations

- **Edit text** must match what’s on screen (WYSIWYG), including motion-pinned frame.
- Entering edit on chapter/caption: **no white flash** — show composed card/plate first.
- Drag handles: only grip/card starts drag — **text selection in inputs must not** start card drag.

## Tests

- `copyEdit.test.ts`, `plateContentSave.test.ts`, shared `kit/lib/copyEdit.test.mjs` when changing serialization.

## Verify manually

1. Type in Content pane — caret stable, inspector doesn’t flash.
2. Edit multi-line title on open plate — height unchanged after entering edit.
3. Save → scrub away → back — copy and layout unchanged.
